<resources>

    <!--
      Autumn in the dark.

      Built from Autumn's own hues rather than a neutral charcoal: the page is #121A21, which
      is the day text colour #2B3545 pushed dark, so the app still reads as blue-grey and teal
      instead of becoming a different application at night.

      The teal gets LIGHTER, not darker. #0A9396 is tuned against white and falls below 4.5:1
      on a dark page, so accents become #2BB3A8 and headings #4FD1C5. Reusing a brand colour
      at its daylight value is the usual way dark mode goes wrong.

      Pure black is avoided throughout. Black is what made the Tree unreadable when this was a
      DayNight theme with no night palette, and on OLED it erases card edges entirely.

      Four groups deliberately have NO night variant:

        month_band_*        All twelve were tuned to carry white text, so they are already
                            mid-dark and saturated and sit correctly on a dark card.
        nav_active,         The bottom bar is navy in both modes, so what sits on it does not
        nav_inactive,       change. The Quicknote bolt stays #FFD400 for the same reason.
        nav_quicknote
        tl_pill,            Backgrounds whose paired text colour is set somewhere this file
        cal_day_selected    cannot see. Left light so dark text on them stays legible; a
        _text               guess here would be a contrast bug rather than a shade people
                            disagree about.

      The Timeline HTML export needs nothing here and gets nothing: HtmlExport contains no
      R.color reference at all, its colours are hardcoded CSS. So the export stays light
      whatever the app does, which is right for a document you may print or send on. The tl_*
      colours below are for the native Timeline views, which are a different thing.
    -->

    <!-- Inherited Markor names -->
    <color name="colorPrimary">@color/primary_dark</color>
    <color name="primary_text">@color/white</color>
    <color name="secondary_text">@color/dark__secondary_text</color>
    <color name="file">@color/dark__file</color>
    <color name="folder">@color/dark__folder</color>
    <color name="background">@color/dark__background</color>
    <color name="background_2">@color/dark__background_2</color>
    <color name="textActionBarColor">@color/dark__background_2</color>
    <color name="textActionIconColor">@color/white</color>

    <!-- Window background, and the note field that was carrying literals -->
    <color name="screen_bg">#121A21</color>
    <color name="surface_card">#1C2730</color>
    <color name="date_selector">#2BB3A8</color>
    <color name="icon_on_surface">#C6D2DE</color>

    <!--
      colorAccent, which every dialog uses for CANCEL, OK and DONE, and which the date
      picker uses for the selected-day circle. The day value #44546A is a dark slate: on the
      dark dialog background it measures 1.30:1, which is not low contrast so much as
      invisible. #A8C0DC is 5.38:1 on the same background.

      It stays in the same blue-slate family rather than becoming the teal, because these
      are system dialog buttons rather than Autumn's own chrome, and the teal reads as a
      content accent everywhere else in the app.
    -->
    <color name="accent">#A8C0DC</color>
    <color name="tl_entry_field_bg">#16202A</color>
    <color name="note_field_bg">#241F12</color>
    <color name="note_field_border">#6E5B2A</color>

